> Do you mean "That <food> was tainted! You feel deathly sick"? That 
> means that the monster was killed a long time ago, and the corpse has 
> gone rotten. This will kill you in a few turns unless you have some 
> means of curing sickness. You should try to eat fresh (newly killed) 
> corpses and not old ones.

The two are often confused because the cause of death for "tainted" food is
"food poisoning", which does _not_ come from eating poisonous corpses.

Generally, the rule is to somehow learn which corpses are actually
poisonous (watch what your pet eats and use common sense [a critter that
has a poisonous sting attack is likely to leave a poisonous corpse, similar
monsters have similar properties, ...]) and eat the save ones as soon as
you've killed them. Even when you're not hungry. Make this a habit, and you
with prayer as an emergency, you won't starve.

